          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Then $U_s^2=\\mathrm{id}$ for every $s$, and the assignment $(\\varepsilon,r)\\cdot s:=U_s(\\varepsilon,r)$ extends to a well-defined **right action** of $W$ on $\\{\\pm1\\}\\times T$ (so $(\\varepsilon,r)\\cdot1=(\\varepsilon,r)$ and $(\\varepsilon,r)\\cdot(wv)=((\\varepsilon,r)\\cdot w)\\cdot v$).",
