        },
        {
          "id": "3.1",
          "claim": "**The descent characterisation and length additivity.** For the three minimal representatives $d=1$, $d=s_2$ and $d=s_2s_1$, the table of [F3] gives $\\ell(s_1\\cdot1)=\\ell(s_1)=1>0=\\ell(1)$, $\\ell(s_1s_2)=2>1=\\ell(s_2)$ and $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=3>2=\\ell(s_2s_1)$, so each of them satisfies the characterisation $\\ell(s_1d)>\\ell(d)$ of [F1]. The additivity identity of [F1] for $u=s_1\\in W_J$ reads $\\ell(s_1d)=\\ell(s_1)+\\ell(d)$ for the minimal $d$; at $d=s_2$ this is $\\ell(s_1s_2)=1+1=2$ and at $d=s_2s_1$ it is $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=1+2=3$, the two values asserted in the statement.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
